# site/public/_headers -- P2-S1-T05 (08 S4.4). Cloudflare's static-asset header rules; Astro copies public/ into the
# build, so this ships as dist/_headers. tools/build/manifest.py (S13) checks the first two rules are here.
#
# /data/* holds only content-hashed files (/data/<name>.<sha8>.json, written by `bench build` and copied by S13, which
# refuses anything else there), so a file at a URL never changes and may be cached for a year.
# /build-manifest.json is the stable URL that names them, so it is short-lived.
# /data/latest/<name>.json has no rule: no file is built there, and the Worker's 302 (site/worker/data-latest.ts) sets
# its own max-age=300, because these rules do not apply to a response the Worker writes.
/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/build-manifest.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

# /ns/* -- P4-S6-T01 (08 S5.8): the croissant-benchmark namespace, its context.jsonld and the page documenting it. The
# path is versioned and v1 only ever gains terms, so a week; not immutable, because it gains them until the extension
# is proposed, and its host is still a placeholder. tests/build/test_croissant_context.py checks this rule.
/ns/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
